irection":"bearish","stage":"forming","confidence":"medium","neckline":3.7,"confirm":"a daily close below the ~$3.70 neckline","invalidate":"a close back above the ~$4.70 level of the right shoulder","target":"~$2.14","explanation":"The pattern shows a left shoulder peaking around $4.84 on May 28, a higher head at $5.26 on June 2, and a developing right shoulder peaking around $3.89 on June 8. The neckline is formed by the troughs around $3.70.","signal":"A confirmed Head and Shoulders pattern could signal a significant bearish reversal, with price potentially dropping towards the measured move target.","builtAt":"2026-06-10T13:36:50.130Z"}},"fundamentals":{"name":"KULR Technology Group, Inc.","longBusinessSummary":"KULR Technology Group, Inc., through its subsidiary, KULR Technology Corporation, designs and builds advanced battery systems for autonomous platforms, digital infrastructure, and e-mobility and space. It provides battery production, internal short circuit battery cells and devices, patented thermal runaway shield technology (TRS), phase change material (PCM) heatsinks, and KULR SafeCases, and exoskeleton devices. The company also offers space batteries; air batteries; custom battery design; battery solutions, including trigger cells and ISC-D and SafeX Safe storage solutions; thermal solutions, including fiber thermal interface and cathodes; and testing solutions that include cell screening and cycling, module cycling, thermal desktop and SINDA/FLUINT, and abuse testing and calorimetry. Additionally, the company provides KULR VIBE, a software-driven precision balancing and vibration reduction solution designed for rotary systems and Xero VibeFan, an ultimate cooling solution for AI farms, data centres, and server environments. Its technologies are used in space, aerospace, defence, telecom, and other critical infrastructure. KULR Technology Group, Inc. has a strategic collaboration with Robinson Helicopter Company, Inc. to develop battery system for an eR66 battery-electric helicopter demonstrator. The company was formerly known as KT High-Tech Marketing, Inc. and changed its name to KULR Technology Group, Inc. in August 2018. The company was founded in 2013 and is headquartered in Webster, Texas.","industry":"Electronic Components","sector":"Technology","marketCap":170688944,"trailingPE":null,"forwardPE":null,"pegRatio":null,"priceToBook":1.8044009,"priceToSales":9.192528,"profitMargin":0,"operatingMargin":-152.38401,"grossMargin":-0.784,"returnOnEquity":-77.298,"returnOnAssets":-25.074,"revenueGrowthYoy":97.89999999999999,"earningsGrowthYoy":null,"earningsQuarterlyGrowthYoy":null,"debtToEquity":6.722,"currentRatio":1.688,"quickRatio":1.305,"freeCashFlow":-23502010,"operatingCashFlow":-43962404,"totalCash":7676308,"totalDebt":6357675,"revenue":18568228,"dividendYield":null,"payoutRatio":0,"beta":2.222,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":10.56,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":1.94,"targetMeanPrice":8,"targetHighPrice":8,"targetLowPrice":8,"recommendationKey":"none","numberOfAnalystOpinions":1,"analystRevisions":null,"lastQuarter":{"date":"2025-09-30","period":"-2q","epsActual":-0.179,"epsEstimate":-0.08,"surprisePct":-123.75},"earningsHistory":[{"date":"2025-03-31","period":"-4q","epsActual":-0.4928,"epsEstimate":-0.08,"surprisePct":-516},{"date":"2025-06-30","period":"-3q","epsActual":0.2588,"epsEstimate":-0.08,"surprisePct":423.50000000000006},{"date":"2025-09-30","period":"-2q","epsActual":-0.179,"epsEstimate":-0.08,"surprisePct":-123.75}],"revenueHistory":[{"date":"2025-03-31","value":2448606},{"date":"2025-06-30","value":3972997},{"date":"2025-09-30","value":6884840},{"date":"2025-12-31","value":2863961},{"date":"2026-03-31","value":4846430}],"grossProfitHistory":[{"date":"2025-03-31","value":206345},{"date":"2025-06-30","value":713710},{"date":"2025-09-30","value":628880},{"date":"2025-12-31","value":-777963},{"date":"2026-03-31","value":1417292}],"netIncomeHistory":[{"date":"2025-03-31","value":-18806658},{"date":"2025-06-30","value":